{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I spread.</b> Rabbi Moses the Kohen says that the first verse concerns the nations of the world, and the meaning is that even to the nations who were not called by My name I was sought, and to the peoples I spread My hands, and the meaning is that I will accept them." "<b>The way.</b> It carries over to itself and afterward to the people with it, and likewise 'the way, a way not good,' like 'and the tree of knowledge, good and evil' <small>(Genesis 2:9)</small>:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {0 "The lemma reads נדרשתי but the corrector's note צ\"ל פרשתי indicates the text should read פרשתי; both forms appear in the body of the comment. Translated as 'I spread' for פרשתי and 'I was sought' for נדרשתי."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:59.658081874Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}